{"id":10886,"date":"2024-01-11T17:05:22","date_gmt":"2024-01-12T01:05:22","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=10886"},"modified":"2024-08-13T20:03:23","modified_gmt":"2024-08-14T03:03:23","slug":"0-7-trimming-jrotc","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-7-trimming-jrotc\/","title":{"rendered":"0.7: Trimming (JROTC ed.)"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221325ce440\" name=\"6a221325ce440\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is Trimming?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Each drone has a gyroscope (gyro) sensor that helps the drone stabilize and center itself during flight. Occasionally, you might see your drone drift during takeoff or during flight commands. Some variation is normal, but if your drone needs some extra help to perform some flight movements correctly, you may need to trim the drone. Watch the video, then review the steps on trimming below.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Note: Although CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) may be a different color, all the information presented in this video still applies.<\/strong>[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/VmoBX3B_LCg&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221325ce555\" name=\"6a221325ce555\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>How to Trim With the Controller<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You will use the directional pads on the controller to trim. Always trim in the opposite direction than the drift.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7517&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221325ce5b2\" name=\"6a221325ce5b2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Practice<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To see the effects of trim, set roll and pitch trim to positive 100. In another lesson, you will learn more about these terms. First, press the &#8220;up&#8221; key on your controller until the pitch value reaches 100.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11212&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Then press the &#8220;right&#8221; key on your controller until the roll value reaches 100.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11213&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Now, takeoff and try to use the joysticks to move around. What do you notice? The drone should be moving towards the front and to the right with each movement. This is an extreme example, but it demonstrates the effects of trimming. Bring the trim values back to 0 by pressing instead the &#8220;down&#8221; and &#8220;left&#8221; directional buttons.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221325ce60d\" name=\"6a221325ce60d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Drifting Up or Down<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You have probably already noticed that there is no option to trim for throttle. Sometimes while flying, you may notice CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) drift up or down even if you are not controlling the throttle, especially when programming.<\/p>\n<p>If CoDrone EDU is drifting up or down, it may be because you are flying in an environment that isn\u2019t completely flat (such as a classroom with tables, chairs, or other furniture). This is because the drone\u2019s internal sensors are trying to maintain a constant height over the surface directly below. For example, if you take off on the ground and fly over a table, CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) may try to compensate for the change in height by throttling up.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11029&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]The opposite effect can happen if you take off from a table then fly over the edge, which is why we always recommend taking off from the floor. CoDrone EDU may throttle down to adjust.<\/p>\n<p>If you notice this kind of &#8220;drift&#8221;, it&#8217;s normal. As a challenge, you can write code to account for this height adjustment or experiment with the height sensor.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221325ce671\" name=\"6a221325ce671\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Next Steps<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Let&#8217;s review! In this lesson, you reviewed how to troubleshoot drifting by using the trim feature on the controller. Remember these tips:<\/div>\n<ul>\n<li>The directional pads on the controller are used to trim.<\/li>\n<li>Always trim in the opposite direction.<\/li>\n<li>If you swap a drone and controller, always check trim settings.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div>In the next and final lesson, you will learn drone maintenance trips.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 6 What is Trimming? [vc_column_text]Each drone has a gyroscope (gyro) sensor that helps the drone stabilize and center itself during flight. Occasionally, you might see your drone drift&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-7-trimming-jrotc\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":11245,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":10878,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[14401,2111,2110],"class_list":["post-10886","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-remote-control","lesson-tag-trimming","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/10886","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":20,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/10886\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12517,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/10886\/revisions\/12517"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/11245"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=10886"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=10886"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=10886"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}